## What to do

### Problem
Railway rolling deploys cause old and new containers to overlap on the same volume. The old code can write 'pending' records that overwrite the new code's properly-scored records. RESET_DB is ineffective because both containers are running simultaneously.

### Solution: add a post-startup cleanup step

1. In `src/lib/db.ts`, add a new function `rescorePendingActivities`:
```ts
export function getPendingActivities(): ActivityLogEntry[] {
  const db = getDb()
  const rows = db.prepare(
    'SELECT id, did, rkey, uri, title, score, tier, breakdown, test_signals, labeled_at FROM activities WHERE tier = ?'
  ).all('pending') as Array<Record<string, unknown>>
  return rows.map(rowToEntry)
}

export function deleteActivity(did: string, rkey: string): void {
  const db = getDb()
  db.prepare('DELETE FROM activities WHERE did = ? AND rkey = ?').run(did, rkey)
}
```

2. In `src/labeler/start.ts`, after the tap consumer starts (after line 92), add a cleanup step:
```ts
// 5b. Clean up any stale pending records from previous deploys
import { getPendingActivities, deleteActivity } from '../lib/db'
const pendingRecords = getPendingActivities()
if (pendingRecords.length > 0) {
  logger.warn({ count: pendingRecords.length }, 'Deleting stale pending records — they will be re-scored on next tap event')
  for (const record of pendingRecords) {
    deleteActivity(record.did, record.rkey)
  }
}
```

This deletes pending records on startup. Tap will re-discover these DIDs and re-score them fresh since the consumer uses INSERT OR REPLACE.

