## What to do
Fix 4 bugs in server.ts. Addresses: hyperlabel-8jy, hyperlabel-ben, hyperlabel-00c, hyperlabel-ijk, hyperlabel-d97.

### 1. Add ORDER BY id ASC to fetchCurrentLabels (P1 — 8jy)
Change:
```sql
SELECT val, neg FROM labels WHERE uri = ? ORDER BY id ASC
```
Without ordering, the neg/pos replay logic can produce wrong results.

### 2. Add per-URI mutex to applyQualityLabel (P2 — ben, 00c)
During backfill, two concurrent events for the same record URI can both read 'no label', both skip negation, and both write — creating duplicate label rows.

Add a simple per-URI lock using a Map of Promises:
```ts
const uriLocks = new Map<string, Promise<void>>()

export async function applyQualityLabel(recordUri: string, labelIdentifier: string): Promise<void> {
  // Wait for any in-flight operation on this URI
  const existing = uriLocks.get(recordUri)
  const operation = (existing ?? Promise.resolve()).then(async () => {
    // ... existing logic unchanged ...
  }).finally(() => {
    // Clean up lock if we're still the latest
    if (uriLocks.get(recordUri) === operation) {
      uriLocks.delete(recordUri)
    }
  })
  uriLocks.set(recordUri, operation)
  return operation
}
```

### 3. Add try/catch inside negateAllDIDLabels per-DID loop (P2 — ijk)
Wrap the inner loop body in try/catch so one failing DID doesn't abort the entire migration:
```ts
for (const row of result.rows) {
  const did = row['uri'] as string
  try {
    const activeLabels = await fetchCurrentLabels(did)
    // ... existing negate logic ...
  } catch (err) {
    logger.error({ err, did }, 'Failed to negate DID-level labels, continuing')
  }
}
```

### 4. Validate labelIdentifier in applyQualityLabel (P2 — d97)
At the top of applyQualityLabel, before any DB operations:
```ts
if (!QUALITY_LABEL_IDENTIFIERS.includes(labelIdentifier)) {
  logger.error({ uri: recordUri, label: labelIdentifier }, 'Rejected unknown label identifier')
