Review of hyperlabel-3lj found an error-handling gap in `negateAllDIDLabels` (server.ts lines 28-47).

The function iterates over all stale DID-level label rows and calls `labelerServer.createLabels()` for each. There is no try/catch inside the loop. If `createLabels` throws for any single DID (e.g. a transient DB error, a malformed DID, a network hiccup), the entire function throws and all remaining DIDs in the list are never processed. On the next startup the same DID will be retried, but any DIDs that came after it in the result set will also be skipped again.

Since this runs at startup before the tap consumer starts, a persistent failure here will also block the tap consumer from ever starting (the error propagates up through `main()` and crashes the process).

**Fix:** Wrap the per-DID block in a try/catch, log the error, and continue to the next DID:
```ts
for (const row of result.rows) {
  const did = row['uri'] as string
  try {
    const activeLabels = await fetchCurrentLabels(did)
    // ... negate ...
  } catch (err) {
    logger.error({ err, did }, 'Failed to negate stale DID-level labels — skipping')
  }
}
```

