In `src/lib/scorer.ts` lines 46-50, the 'title duplicates start of short description' check uses `titleWords.length > 10` where `titleWords` is the joined string of the first 4 words. This checks the **character** length of the joined string, not the number of words.

**Impact:** Titles composed of short single-letter words (e.g. `'A B C D'`) produce a `titleWords` string of `'a b c d'` (7 chars), which fails the `> 10` guard and the copy-paste signal is never fired — even when the title perfectly duplicates the start of the short description.

**Reproduction:**
```ts
const title = 'A B C D'
const shortDesc = 'A B C D is a great project'
const titleWords = title.trim().toLowerCase().split(/\s+/).slice(0, 4).join(' ')
// titleWords = 'a b c d' (7 chars)
// titleWords.length > 10 → false → signal NOT fired
// Expected: signal should fire (title is first 4 words of shortDesc)
```

